    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d651">

                <pb facs="0975" n="871" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg871"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">884.6461 Tsana Dam/377: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt (Jardine) to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-01-21T11:00:00+02:00">January 21,
                            1933—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 21—6:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3. Following telegram has been sent by me to Southard.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“British plan to have Egyptians pay the entire cost Tsana initially has
                        raised storm of protest following public disclosures regarding plans and
                        these have now been abandoned in favor of a request to the Emperor for
                        permission for a further survey and report by the White Company. Lardner
                        agreeable to this and is bringing under seal for your information copy of a
                        detailed despatch to Department<anchor n="22" xml:id="d651-f1"/> regarding
                        latest developments. Am repeating to the Department.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jardine</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d651-f1" n="22" xml:id="d651-f1-content">
                <p>Presumably despatch No. 645 of January 20, 1933, from the Minister in Egypt; not
                    printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
